results.solution:
We apply the distributive property repeatedly: \begin{align*}
(q-5)(3r+6) &= q(3r+6) - 5(3r+6)\\
&= q\cdot 3r + q\cdot 6 - 5\cdot 3r - 5\cdot 6\\
&= \boxed{3qr + 6q - 15r -30}.
\end{align*}

We just plug into our function definitions given in the problem:

\begin{align*}
f(g(7)) + g(f(3)) &= f(7 + 7) + g(3^2 - 1) \\
&= f(14) + g(8) = (14^2 - 1) + (8 + 7) \\
&= 195 + 15 = \boxed{210}
\end{align*}

