P_A &= \tfrac12 P_J + \tfrac12 P_K = \tfrac12\left(\tfrac12\right) + \tfrac12(1) = \tfrac14 + \tfrac12 = \tfrac34.
\end{aligned}
\]

Thus the probability that a log that starts in pond \(A\) ends up in pond \(B\) is  

\[
\boxed{\tfrac34}.
\]<|im_end|>

