The prism has equilateral‐triangle bases of side \(12\) and height \(16\).  
Place the bottom base in the plane \(z=0\) and the top base in the plane \(z=16\).

\[
\begin{aligned}
A&=(0,0,0), &
B&=(12,0,0), &
C&=(6,6\sqrt3,0),\\[2mm]
D&=(0,0,16), &
E&=(12,0,16), &
F&=(6,6\sqrt3,16).
\end{aligned}
\]

Thus the three lateral edges are \(AD,\;BE,\;CF\) (each of length \(16\)).

---

### 1.  Coordinates of the cut points  

* On \(DE\) we have \(DM=4\).  Since \(DE=12\),

\[
M=\Bigl(\frac{4}{12}\cdot12,\;0,\;16\Bigr)=(4,0,16).
\]

* On \(DF\) we have \(DN=2\),

\[
N=\Bigl(\frac{2}{12}\cdot6,\;\frac{2}{12}\cdot6\sqrt3,\;16\Bigr)=(1, \sqrt3, 16).
\]

* On \(CA\) we have \(CQ=8\).  Since \(CA=12\),

\[
Q=\Bigl(\frac{8}{12}\cdot6,\;\frac{8}{12}\cdot6\sqrt3,\;0\Bigr)=(4,4\sqrt3,0).
\]

* On \(CB\) we are not given a distance, but the plane through \(M,N,Q\) meets the edge \(CB\) at a point \(P\).  
Write a point of \(CB\) as  

\[
P=(12-6t,\;6\sqrt3\,t,\;0),\qquad 0\le t\le1 .
\]

The plane through \(M,N,Q\) has equation  

\[
x-2y+2z=4 .
\]

Substituting the coordinates of \(P\) gives  

\[
(12-6t)-2(6\sqrt3\,t)+0=4\;\Longrightarrow\;t=\frac{4}{3(2+\sqrt3)} .
\]

Hence  

\[
P=\Bigl(12-6t,\;6\sqrt3\,t,\;0\Bigr)
   =\Bigl(12-\frac{8}{2+\sqrt3},\;\frac{8\sqrt3}{2+\sqrt3},\;0\Bigr).
\]

---

### 2.  Volume of the cut–off solid  

The solid \(QPCDMN\) is bounded by the plane \(x-2y+2z=4\) and the three faces that meet at the edge \(CD\):
the top face \(z=16\), the bottom face \(z=0\), and the lateral face \(x=0\) (the face \(CAFD\)).  
Its projection onto the \(xy\)-plane is the quadrilateral with vertices  

\[
(0,0),\;(4,4\sqrt3),\;(12-6t,\;6\sqrt3\,t),\;(4,0).
\]

Using the shoelace formula,

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Area} &=\frac12\Bigl|
0\cdot4\sqrt3+4\cdot6\sqrt3\,t+(12-6t)\cdot0+4\cdot0\\
&\qquad -\bigl(0\cdot4+4\sqrt3\,(12-6t)+6\sqrt3\,t\cdot4+0\cdot0\bigr)
\Bigr|\\[2mm]
&=24\sqrt3\,t .
\end{aligned}
\]

Since \(t=\dfrac{4}{3(2+\sqrt3)}\),

\[
\text{Area}=24\sqrt3\cdot\frac{4}{3(2+\sqrt3)}
          =\frac{32\sqrt3}{\,2+\sqrt3}
          =32(2-\sqrt3).
\]

The height of the solid (the distance between the two parallel faces \(z=0\) and \(z=16\)) is \(16\).  
Hence

\[
V=\text{Area}\times 16
   =32(2-\sqrt3)\times16
   =512\,(2-\sqrt3).
\]

---

\[
\boxed{512\,(2-\sqrt3)}
\]<|im_end|>

