dot("$P$", P, SE);
dot("$Q$", Q, S);
dot((-1,P.y));
dot((-1,Q.y));
[/asy]

Since $P$ lies on the parabola, $PF$ is equal to the distance from $P$ to the directrix, which is $x_1 + a.$  Similarly, $QF$ is equal to the distance from $Q$ to the directrix, which is $x_2 + a.$  Therefore,
\[PQ = x_1 + x_2 + 2a.\]Hence, $c_1 + c_2 + c_3 = 1 + 1 + 2 = \boxed{4}.$

From the given equation, $c - a = 2(b - c).$  Then $c - a = 2b - 2c.$  Solving for $c,$ we find
\[c = \frac{a + 2b}{3} = \frac{(1 + i) + 2(4 + 7i)}{3} = \boxed{3 + 5i}.\][asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C;

A = (1,1);
B = (4,7);
C = interp(A,B,2/3);

draw(A--B);

dot("$a$", A, NW);
dot("$b$", B, NW);
dot("$c$", C, NW);
