The ray \(AB\) lies on the interior side of \(AD\) while the ray \(AC\) lies on the exterior side, so the two rays are on opposite sides of \(AD\).  
Therefore the angle between them is the supplement of the sum of the interior angle of the heptagon and the right angle:

\[
\angle BAC = 180^\circ -\left(\frac{900}{7}^\circ + 90^\circ\right)
          = 180^\circ - \frac{1530}{7}^\circ
          = \frac{2520-1530}{7}^\circ
          = \frac{990}{7}^\circ .
\]

Thus  

\[
\boxed{\frac{990}{7}}.
\]<|im_end|>

