Begin by simplifying the left side by grouping consecutive pairs of terms: $$(x-2x)+(3x-4x)+(5x-6x)+(7x-8x)+(9x-10x)=50$$ Now simplify, and solve for $x$: \begin{align*}
-x-x-x-x-x&=50\\
\Rightarrow\qquad -5x&=50\\
\Rightarrow\qquad x&=\boxed{-10}
\end{align*}

Notice that the two fractions have the same denominator, so we can add them. Addition is commutative, so we can rearrange the terms to get  \begin{align*}
\frac{k-3}{2} +\frac{3k+1}{2}+3k+1 &=\frac{4k-2}{2}+3k+1 \\
&=2k-1+3k+1 \\
&=\boxed{5k}.\end{align*}

